{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/php","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:10.934Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/php/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/php/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official PHP image for CBL-Mariner.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is PHP?\n\nPHP is a server-side scripting language designed for web development, but which can also be used as a general-purpose programming language. PHP can be added to straight HTML or it can be used with a variety of templating engines and web frameworks. PHP code is usually processed by an interpreter, which is either implemented as a native module on the web-server or as a common gateway interface (CGI).\n\nSee: [wikipedia.org/wiki/PHP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PHP)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `8`\n- `8-cm2.0`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to php version, Mariner build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a simple PHP app\n\n`1.` Create a Dockerfile to generate a new image that includes the necessary content.\n\n    FROM mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/php:8\n\n    COPY . /usr/src/myapp\n    WORKDIR /usr/src/myapp\n\n    # Start the app.\n    CMD [ \"php\", \"./your-script.php\" ]\n\n\n`2.` Build and run your container image.\n\n    docker build -t php-app-image .\n    docker run -it --rm --name running-php-app php-app-image\n\nThe default container startup command is `\"php\", \"-a\"`.\n\n### Run a single PHP script\n\nFor many simple, single file projects, you may find it inconvenient to write a complete Dockerfile. In such cases, you can run a php script (named my-script.php in the example below) by using the Mariner based PHP docker image directly:\n\n    docker run -it --rm --name running-php-script -v \"$PWD\":/usr/src/myapp -w /usr/src/myapp mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/php:8 php my-script.php\n\n### Run PHP repl environment\n\nYou may want to simply run the interactive shell that comes with php by launching it when the container starts. In such case, you can run php by using the Mariner based php docker image directly. The following command will launch the virtual environment that php comes with:\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/php:8\n\n### Launch Mariner shell\n\nThe PHP image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to launch Mariner shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/php:8 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:49:25.7066844+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"281K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"8.1-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:b5409d4375740a1d5c26e53fa10f570599797ec00b5c6c862f08b621bac3ba08","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:33:56.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"8.1","digest":"sha256:b5409d4375740a1d5c26e53fa10f570599797ec00b5c6c862f08b621bac3ba08","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:33:49.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"8-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:b5409d4375740a1d5c26e53fa10f570599797ec00b5c6c862f08b621bac3ba08","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:33:36.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"8","digest":"sha256:b5409d4375740a1d5c26e53fa10f570599797ec00b5c6c862f08b621bac3ba08","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:33:25.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"8.1.34-1-cm2.0.20260311","digest":"sha256:b5409d4375740a1d5c26e53fa10f570599797ec00b5c6c862f08b621bac3ba08","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:33:17.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"8.1.34-1-cm2.0.20260311-arm64","digest":"sha256:8615be726114a9c350e556d1c20f32daaa688ae5c6f96df18361